// fs2_qrinf — the quarter-rate classes with more than two micro-ops in flight (shader_core_fs2 QR_INF = 4):
// whole-vec4 operations of one class back to back on independent registers (a vec4 is four micro-ops 4 cycles
// apart, a SIN / COS or an SFU result ~21 cycles after its issue: the class fills), every class in turn and mixed, results
// used at once, a later write over an earlier one of the same class whole and in part (WAW), and the converts and the
// integer multiply chained. What it checks: the results come back to the right register and component in the order they
// were issued (a collector's meta queue of QR_INF, the shared result queue of 4 x QR_INF) at 4 and at 8 warps, and the
// same with QR_INF = 2 (tb_fs2 -Defines TB_QRINF2).
// Golden: python3 tools/isa64.py fs2 tests/fs2_qrinf.sasm --exact-rcp; tb_fs2 with +TOL_8.
LDV    r1, 8                         // per lane and component, 0.25 .. 3.25
LDP    r2, 1                         // 0.75
LDP    r3, 3                         // 1.25
// SIN / COS: 16 micro-ops of the class back to back
SIN    r4, r1
COS    r5, r1
SIN    r6, r2
COS    r7, -r1
// the SFU: every operation, plain and times an operand
RCP    r8, r1
RSQRT  r9, r1
LOG2   r10, r1
EXP2   r11, r2
SQRT   r12, r1
DIV    r13, r3, r1
// converts and the integer multiply, chained
FLR    r14, r1
CEIL   r15, r1
FTOI   r16, r1
ITOF   r17, r16
IMUL   r18, r16, r16
IMUL   r19, r18, r16
ITOF   r20, r19
// results used at once
ADD    r21, r4, r5
MUL    r22, r8, r9
SUB    r23, r14, r17
// a later write over an earlier one of the same class: whole, then in part
SIN    r24, r1
SIN    r24, r2
RCP    r25, r1
RCP    r25.xy, r3.xy
FLR    r26, r1
CEIL   r26.zw, r1.zw
ADD    r27, r24, r25
// the classes mixed, a component each, then each class's result into the next one's argument
SIN    r28.x, r1.x
RCP    r28.y, r1.y
FLR    r28.z, r1.z
COS    r28.w, r1.w
SIN    r29, r28
RCP    r30, r29
FLR    r31, r30
END
